{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/877258-is-the-caul-singular-or-an-example-of-what-a-lunar-domain-might-be-like","id":877258,"title":"Is the Caul singular or an example of what a Lunar domain might be like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-28T19:45:44-07:00","id":877258,"title":"Is the Caul singular or an example of what a Lunar domain might be like?","content":"So, Lookshy sort of started as an example of what a Dragon-Blooded-run state outside the Realm might look like, and morphed into the only Dragon-Blooded-run state that existed (well, besides Cherak, but nobody paid attention to Cherak).<br /> <br /> Tepet Ejava sort of started as an example of what a claimant to the Empress' throne might look like, and morphed into the only claimant besides Little Pink.<br /> <br /> Which is the Caul? Is it a sample of the sort of weird, separated-from-the-laws-of-Creation, inhospitable military quagmire separated from Fate that one would just generally expect of a homebrewed, player-run Lunar dominion, or is it a singular achievement that is the sole instance of Lunar infrastructure in the face of Realm hostility? Is it the biggest example of its kind (and then maybe other Lunars have attempted to export its success, to varying degrees of efficacy), or the only one?<br /> <br /> I guess the real million-dinar question is, if my Solar accidentally blows it up, can they get another one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T19:51:50-07:00","id":877261,"title":"","content":"The Caul is singular.<br /> It is what I'd expect of a homebrewed, player-run Lunar domain.<br /> <br /> Just like Tepet Ejava and Mnemon are the only real contenders to the throne unless one of your PCs wants to step up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T20:01:36-07:00","id":877263,"title":"","content":"The Caul is the greatest concentration of the Lunars' power in Creation, but I'd rate the Mountain of the Spider King as the most strategically important of the dominions (that we know of). From a player's perspective, I'd aim for the latter rather than the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T20:05:16-07:00","id":877265,"title":"","content":"And there may be dozens of other Lunar Exalted realms. Heck, Halta could be considered to be the most successful of the Lunar realms because it was created by Lunar Exalted as a sociological experiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T20:11:31-07:00","id":877269,"title":"","content":"I paid attention to Cherak. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Ferem was one of my favourite houses. I was sad that Cherak never got a proper write-up.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I got the impression that the Caul is the greatest Lunar realm. Not the only one, but the most powerful one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T20:20:58-07:00","id":877274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/877258-is-the-caul-singular-or-an-example-of-what-a-lunar-domain-might-be-like?p=877265#post877265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, Halta could be considered to be the most successful of the Lunar realms because it was created by Lunar Exalted as a sociological experiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>(assorted hissing sounds)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T22:53:15-07:00","id":877374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/877258-is-the-caul-singular-or-an-example-of-what-a-lunar-domain-might-be-like?p=877274#post877274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(assorted hissing sounds)</div> </div> </div> </div>Needs more <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CC7iPlnbIkk\" target=\"_blank\">nope</a> to fully convey the feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T23:01:59-07:00","id":877379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/877258-is-the-caul-singular-or-an-example-of-what-a-lunar-domain-might-be-like?p=877263#post877263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caul is the greatest concentration of the Lunars' power in Creation, but I'd rate the Mountain of the Spider King as the most strategically important of the dominions (that we know of). From a player's perspective, I'd aim for the latter rather than the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd enjoy hearing your reasoning on this one. I don't necessarily disagree (the West is only going to become more important, economically, moving forward assuming a New World model of relative economic impact), but I am curious!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T00:44:26-07:00","id":877435,"title":"","content":"The Caul seems an atypical Dominion for a number of reasons. One, the concentration of Lunar activity. Most dominions seem much more individual/small group projects. Two, the religious dimension. The Caul is sacred to both Lunars and Dragon-Blooded. Its conflict isn't JUST about tearing at the Realm (though that's, of course, a huge, huge part of it, given its strategic value), it's also regaining the land where Luna once walked. Three, the... presence of His Divine Lunar Presence. And of course, four, there is the whole &quot;has it's own Loom of Fate and is outside the Sidereals' control&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T00:58:32-07:00","id":877443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/877258-is-the-caul-singular-or-an-example-of-what-a-lunar-domain-might-be-like#post877258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Lookshy sort of started as an example of what a Dragon-Blooded-run state outside the Realm might look like, and morphed into the only Dragon-Blooded-run state that existed (well, besides Cherak, but nobody paid attention to Cherak).<br /> <br /> Tepet Ejava sort of started as an example of what a claimant to the Empress' throne might look like, and morphed into the only claimant besides Little Pink.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that pretty much describes the transition from 1E to 2E. Everythjng that was to benjust one example canonically became the only one there is. Andnit was stuff like that that brought down the coolness of the game. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Which is the Caul? </div> </div> </div>Actually, I dont viewmit as a Lunar Realm at all. More a location of conflict and major plot point. Remember, the cities were Realm controled.<br /> <br /> I look to Ma-Ha-Suchi's realm as a typical Lunar one. Or atmleast a more stereotypical one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess the real million-dinar question is, if my Solar accidentally blows it up, can they get another one? </div> </div> </div>I guess if you have Wyld Shaping Technique and a lot of XP to burn.<br /> <br /> <br /> Btw, where is all this stuff abutnit's own Loom from? I dont recall that, but then again I havnt read the completed version of the Core yet either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T03:18:47-07:00","id":877516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/877258-is-the-caul-singular-or-an-example-of-what-a-lunar-domain-might-be-like?p=877274#post877274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(assorted hissing sounds)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't like that, then explain BOOMERANGS IN A FOREST without Celestial level shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T03:52:16-07:00","id":877533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caul seems an atypical Dominion for a number of reasons. One, the concentration of Lunar activity. Most dominions seem much more individual/small group projects. Two, the religious dimension. The Caul is sacred to both Lunars and Dragon-Blooded. Its conflict isn't JUST about tearing at the Realm (though that's, of course, a huge, huge part of it, given its strategic value), it's also regaining the land where Luna once walked. Three, the... presence of His Divine Lunar Presence. And of course, four, there is the whole &quot;has it's own Loom of Fate and is outside the Sidereals' control&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, I think the Caul is something that barely qualifies as a Lunar Dominion as the term is defined by the core; I see it more as a highly noteworthy example of what a Lunar might be doing when <i>not</i> part of the Silver Pact, which deserves some attention as well. After all, not being in the Silver Pact appears to be more than just an edge case that isn't worth focusing on when it gets given so much attention in the Lunar summary and (to my reading) two of the major Lunar non-players characters are part of that category. Still, I think that making other such places the Caul in miniature would diminish its impact a bit. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">explain BOOMERANGS IN A FOREST without Celestial level shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh, we might as well; it's not as if the intervention of Lunars is evident in any other way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T06:49:12-07:00","id":877637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/877258-is-the-caul-singular-or-an-example-of-what-a-lunar-domain-might-be-like?p=877379#post877379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd enjoy hearing your reasoning on this one. I don't necessarily disagree (the West is only going to become more important, economically, moving forward assuming a New World model of relative economic impact), but I am curious!</div> </div> </div> </div>Aum-Ashatra managed to wrap his hands around one of the North's major caravan routes. It's the North, so sailing past the road is an iffy proposition at the best of times, and the other, smaller roads are likely to be filled with your choice of barbarians, Fair Folk, undead, or any other manner of horror that you probably don't want to think about. If he wants to wreck the economy of everything west of Cherak and affect the course of the Realm Civil War in the northern satrapies, he can probably find some way to do it. The Black Shale Road is more likely to carry luxury goods than essentials, but the Great Houses and the Guild are going to have to make up for their losses somehow. On top of that, every caravan he assaults and seizes gives him more resources he can use to back other Lunars' barbarian hordes. That would give him a tremendous amount of political power and influence among other Lunars. If he wants to step out of his caves and wage a serious war against the satrapies, shit is going to go down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T07:40:20-07:00","id":877671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/877258-is-the-caul-singular-or-an-example-of-what-a-lunar-domain-might-be-like?p=877443#post877443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, where is all this stuff abutnit's own Loom from? I dont recall that, but then again I havnt read the completed version of the Core yet either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Early early sneak peaks from Devs. I can't recall if it was discussed during the Kickstarter (feels right) or just a Dev comment on the forums. That factoid is definitely 2-3 years old, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T07:45:21-07:00","id":877676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/877258-is-the-caul-singular-or-an-example-of-what-a-lunar-domain-might-be-like?p=877637#post877637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aum-Ashatra managed to wrap his hands around one of the North's major caravan routes. It's the North, so sailing past the road is an iffy proposition at the best of times, and the other, smaller roads are likely to be filled with your choice of barbarians, Fair Folk, undead, or any other manner of horror that you probably don't want to think about. If he wants to wreck the economy of everything west of Cherak and affect the course of the Realm Civil War in the northern satrapies, he can probably find some way to do it. The Black Shale Road is more likely to carry luxury goods than essentials, but the Great Houses and the Guild are going to have to make up for their losses somehow. On top of that, every caravan he assaults and seizes gives him more resources he can use to back other Lunars' barbarian hordes. That would give him a tremendous amount of political power and influence among other Lunars. If he wants to step out of his caves and wage a serious war against the satrapies, shit is going to go down.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gives me a few neat ideas for my Southern game; thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T07:46:57-07:00","id":877679,"title":"","content":"Oh man, the desert and fire elementals would make all that so much worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3